AB  - The article is devoted to the use of tire rubber-filled matte in terms of 3D printing process parameters. The article is a prelude to further studies of the correlation between 3D printing parameters for materials such as polyolefins and polyolefins filled with recycled rubber. The publication aims to prove that it is also possible to print from recycled materials with high processing shrinkage on a standard printer, which may have household applications. The goal of the publication was achieved while showing promising results. The strength characteristics tested, for all the tests conducted, decreased after the addition of 20% rubber powder, as would be expected. Young's modulus decreased by about 306 MPa, or 27%. Tensile strength decreased by about 20% after the addition of GTR compared to solid specimens. The bending modulus value for PP/20GTR samples is 316.5 MPa lower than that of PP samples. The impact test showed a decrease of less than 15%.
