AB  - Ultrasonic testing is applied to recycled filament for 3D-printer to evaluate degradation of the filament. 3D printing enables the fabrication of near-net-shaped products with almost no waste materials. Especially, 3D-printer based on fused deposition modeling (FDM) using thermoplastics is widespread because of the simplicity and relatively low manufacturing costs. In addition, filaments containing carbon fibers have also been developed to improve mechanical properties of the products. On the other hand, filament reproduction attracts much attention from view points of economy and ecology. In this paper, to obtain more reliable products by 3D-printer, physical properties of recycled filaments are evaluated based on ultrasonic testing.
