AB  - The study examines the use of polyamide as a viable alternative to replace metals in various industrial applications due to its remarkable properties such as low weight, mechanical strength, and chemical stability. The research highlights the advantages of reinforced variants, such as polyamide 66 or PA-MXD6, in the automotive, aerospace, and electronics industries. Advanced processing methods, including CNC milling, gas-assisted injection molding, and 3D printing, contribute to the production of precise and efficient components. The integration of polyamide into automated processes and material recycling supports circular economy goals and reduces environmental impact. The conclusions emphasize polyamide's role as a versatile material, with emerging applications in robotics, medicine, and space exploration.
