KW  - Mold
KW  - Fused deposition modeling
KW  - Material properties
KW  - Compression test
AB  - [EN] This paper presents the design and validation of molds for concrete test specimens manufactured using 3D printing, to reduce costs and increase versatility in the face of non-standard geometries. PETG was used as the printing material due to its impermeability and compliance with the UNE-EN 12390-1 standard. Different concretes were evaluated, including mixtures with superplasticizing additives and recycled and conventional aggregates. After the additive manufacturing of the molds, an experimental evaluation was carried out to analyze their influence on the mechanical properties of the concrete, comparing them with traditional molds. Compression tests showed that there were no significant differences in the strength obtained, with average values of 42.02 MPa and 36.82 MPa for conventional and printed molds, respectively. The results confirm the technical feasibility of using 3D-printed molds for structural applications, consolidating this technology as an effective alternative in the field of test specimen manufacturing.
