AB  - This work proposes the integration of a variety of critical success factors to implement circular production systems. For this, this study aims to design a novel sustainable management system that allows the integration of VSM into I4.0 technologies for CE purposes. This system also provides new metrics, extends traditional VSM, and explores the use of recycled powder in additive manufacturing, cloud computing, Big Data, Internet of Things (IoT), and cyber-physical systems. The research method combines a scoping literature review and focus groups with academic and industrial experts. From a theoretical point of view, a constructivist theory is used to propose an innovative circular model. The result is a general model that we call “Circular Value Stream Mapping (CVSM) 4.0”. This model is empirically applied with successive focus groups in an I4.0 factory laboratory to produce a specific CVSM 4.0 model. To assess its validity, this specific CVSM 4.0 model is applied to a case study to design a digital recycling factory that uses 3D printing of industrial waste materials to manufacture product subsets for other companies or assembly 4.0 to achieve a final product. The CVSM 4.0 model seeks continuous incremental improvements to linear production systems to achieve CE practices.
