AB  - There is a considerable need for water purification in order to prevent the harm caused to the environment by the harmful and even toxic metals analyzed in the shooting range run-off water in this study. The most harmful metals found are cadmium, nickel, copper, uranium and especially lead, the concentrations of which is remarkably high, exceeding the limit values set for the environment significantly. Herein we report the use of polypropylene based 4D Scavengers (3D-printed filters) containing Dowex 50WX8 ion exchange resin as an active additive for the removal of heavy metals from military shooting range run-off waters. The removal of metals using 4D Scavenger technology was tested and optimized in the laboratory scale followed with the field tests at Finnish Defence Forces shooting range area. The highest recovery rates for heavy metals investigated were obtained using the 4D Scavengers produced by Selective Laser Sintering (SLS) 3D-printing technique with a mixture of polypropylene (~50 µm diameter) and 30 wt% of Dowex 50WX8 200-400 mesh (74-37 m) as a printing material. The maximum adsorption capacity for lead, i.e. the maximum adsorption per gram of scavenger material, was determined using the Langmuir isotherm and resulted in as high as 158.73 mg g-1 (=1.53 meq mL-1). This compares well with the value reported by the manufacturer for Dowex 50WX8 cation exchange resin 176.12 mg g-1 (=1.7 meq mL-1) and shows the effectiveness of 4D Scavengers. In the field tests, as high as 98% recovery rates were obtained for all of the heavy metals investigated. The 4D Scavenger technology enables not only an effective removal of heavy metals from shooting range run-off waters, but also at the same time the recycling of metals the some of which are critical for the industry. Since 4D Scavengers are reusable, this unique technology enables the recovery and recycling of heavy metals in a sustainable way.
