AB  - Poland’s economy recovered from the recession in 1992 and gradually became one of the fastest-growing countries in Central and Eastern Europe.\n\nAfter joining the European Union, the economy has made rapid progress. In 2009, due to the impact of the international financial crisis, the economy declined significantly, but it was still better than most EU countries and the only country in the EU to achieve positive growth.\n\nThe economy continued to grow in 2010, growing by 3.8%, one of the highest rates in the European Union. It attracted $14.2 billion of foreign investment.\n\nAccording to the Doing Business 2013 Annual Report jointly released by the World Bank and the International Finance Corporation, Poland is the EU economy that has made the fastest progress in improving its business environment since 2005.\n\nAre you looking for injection molding suppliers in Poland? We have compiled the top 5 injection molding manufacturers list for you to pick as below:\n\n1. Rosti Poland\n\nLocation: Białystok, Poland\nCompany type: Manufacturing\nYear founded: 1944\nThe number of employees: 200-299\nMain products: Injection Moulding, Injection blow molding, In-mould labeling, liquid silicone rubber\n\nRosti Poland Company Profile\n\nRosti is a global plastic injection molding company and contract manufacturer to some of the world’s leading manufacturers in the packaging, consumer appliances, business machines, home automation, medical and automotive sectors.\n\nRosti has a history of precision plastic injection molding service solutions dating back to 1944. Founded in Denmark by Rolf Fahrenholtz and Stig Jørgensen, Rosti began with the production of buttons using injection molding, shortly after the Second World War. This innovative and relatively new method provided increased production at a lower cost compared to conventional press molding.\n\n2. AKSON\n\nLocation: Grunwaldzka, Poland\nCompany type: Manufacturing\nYear founded: 1996\nThe number of employees: 200-299\nMain products: Injection molds, Blow molds, Blow mandrels\n\nAKSON Company Profile\n\nAKSON is a company closely related to the packaging industry, being primarily a manufacturer of custom injection mold for packaging elements for the following technologies: “Much more than plastic processing tools” this is their motto.\n\nUnderstanding the needs of the market, AKSON not only produces molds for the production of packaging but also designs packaging through all stages of the project, that is development of the packaging idea, shape study, feasibility study, model documentation, optimization, creation of final 3D and 2D documentation and specification of technical requirements.\n\nTheir undoubted achievement is the development and launch of the production of standardized blow mandrels, one of the necessary tools in the packaging production process in the extrusion blow molding technology (EBM). They also have their own plastics processing department specializing in the production of packaging elements by manufacturing injection molding.\n\n3. “ŚLIWA Plastic Injection Molding” Ltd\n\nLocation: Kiel, Poland\nCompany type: Manufacturing\nYear founded: 1981\nThe number of employees: 100-199\nMain products: Injection Molding, Assembly, Pad printing\n\nŚLIWA Plastic Injection Molding Ltd Company Profile\n\n“ŚLIWA Plastic Injection Molding” Ltd. is a family company founded in 1981. At the core of the company is the processing of plastics, in which they specialize from the beginning of their activity.\n\nThey are constantly developing and looking for new business contacts. They offer their clients the highest quality services, which is confirmed by the PN-EN ISO 9001: 2015-10 certificate implemented and maintained since 1999 and the PN-EN ISO 14001: 2015-09 certificate since 2003.\n\nTheir highest standards allow them to cooperate with the automotive industry and the energy industry. This industry is one of the most demanding segments of the market. Thanks to many years of cooperation and experience, they guarantee each client the highest quality of their products.\n\nCurrently, they employ 120 people in the management, technical supervision, quality control, and direct production sectors, who are qualified and experienced staff.. is a family company founded in 1981. At the core of the company is the processing of plastics, in which they specialize from the beginning of their activity.\n\nThey are constantly developing and looking for new business contacts. The strategic production department of the company is the injection molding services department which is confirmed by the PN-EN ISO 9001: 2015-10 certificate implemented and maintained since 1999 and the PN-EN ISO 14001: 2015-09 certificate since 2003.\n\n4. WM\n\nLocation: Łódź, Poland\nCompany type: Manufacturing\nYear founded: 1989\nThe number of employees: 100-199\nMain products: Plastic injection molding, Metal processing\n\nWM Company Profile\n\nThe WM company exists and has been dynamically developing since 1989. Their industry is plastic injection molding services and metal processing. They are a supplier of fully comprehensive solutions from the idea to the finished product. They have a modern, computerized injection shop and a well-equipped tool room.\n\nThey specialize in the production of details with the highest quality requirements and advanced geometry. They employ up to 20 highly qualified employees, trained by technicians from companies such as:” DUPONT”,” HOECHST” or “GEP”. The production process at each stage is subject to the quality control system based on the PN-EN ISO 9001-2009 standard.\n\n5. Molanderplast\n\nLocation: Szczecin, Poland\nCompany type: Manufacturing\nYear founded: 1983\nThe number of employees: 100-199\nMain products: Injection molding, Self-developed products\n\nMolanderplast Company Profile\n\nMolanderplast is a design and production company specializing in injection molding services for plastic products. They have the experience and the know-how, from idea to ready product, to develop and conduct projects where their knowledge of the possibilities of polymers gives the client major profits.\n\nThey have experience in product development in many types of businesses and industrial operations. They are particularly good at materials handling and logistics. Their trays and packages give effective handling and minimum transport volume.\n\nBut their technology can be used in practically any type of business. They give the client better products, simpler production, easier handling, and lower costs. Often it’s all about replacing inappropriate and expensive disposable materials with recyclable injection molded products.\n\nIf you’re looking for more injection molding manufacturers, Also you can choose a China injection mold supplier: Zetar Mold\n\nZetar Mold\n\nLocation: Shanghai, China\nCompany type: Manufacturing\nYear founded: 2005\nThe number of employees: 201-300\nMain product: Plastic Injection Mold, Plastic Injection Molding Manufacturing\nOther products: Injection molding manufacturing, Insert Molding Products, 3D printing, and CNC Prototyping\n\nZetar Company Profile\n\nZetar is a top-end turnkey China injection molding manufacturing company that helps wholesalers and brand owners fulfill their products.\n\nZetar has more than 20 English speakers and 7 experienced mold design engineers (some of them can also speak English) with technique and English communication, which could make sure fluent communication and offer feasible design solutions.\n\nNow total Zetar has mold making shop in-house, with 31 sets of injection molding machines ranging from 60T-1100T. which 6 sets are in the dust-free room(M7 Class), assembly room, and logo printing room. The largest 1100T injection molding machines could produce product weight up to 5100g.\n\nStar also has many certificates: TUV, ISO9001 (quality system certification), TS16949 (certification for auto parts making), and ISO14001 (certification for showing not harming the environment during the whole manufacturing process).\n\nConclusion\n\nFinding a trustworthy manufacturer nowadays is not that easy, especially since there are a lot of new manufacturers that have emerged just to keep up with the trend. But hopefully, our list was able to help you find the injection mold manufacturer that best suits your requirements. It is recommended to do a background check before creating partnerships with manufacturers because they will play a huge part in the success of your business.
